* SALES SUMMARY - SORT THEN REPORT
*
* Two activities.  The SORT copies SALESIN to SALESRT unchanged (only the
* ORDER differs), so the report's columns still trace back to SALESIN's
* bytes through the sort - which is the point of modelling a sort copy as a
* field edge rather than as an opaque step.
*
* SALESRT takes its layout from SALESIN with a library-section COPY, at the
* same byte positions.
*
FILE SALESIN FB(100 1000)
  SL-REGION       1   2 A
  SL-STORE        3   4 N
  SL-SKU          7  10 A
  SL-QTY         17   5 P 0
  SL-AMOUNT      22   7 P 2
*
FILE SALESRT FB(100 1000)
  COPY SALESIN
*
SORT SALESIN TO SALESRT USING (SL-REGION SL-STORE SL-SKU) NAME SORTSALE
*
JOB INPUT SALESRT NAME RPTJOB
  PRINT SALESRPT
*
REPORT SALESRPT LINESIZE 132 SUMMARY
  SEQUENCE SL-REGION SL-STORE
  CONTROL SL-REGION SL-STORE
  SUM SL-QTY SL-AMOUNT
  TITLE 'SALES SUMMARY BY REGION AND STORE'
  HEADING SL-AMOUNT ('SALES' 'AMOUNT')
  LINE SL-REGION SL-STORE SL-SKU SL-QTY SL-AMOUNT
